- equal values down a column :: len(grid) > 1 and any(grid[r][c] == grid[r + 1][c] for r in range(len(grid) - 1) for c in range(len(grid[0]))) :: minimum_operations([[2], [2]])
- no equal values down a column :: len(grid) > 1 and all(grid[r][c] != grid[r + 1][c] for r in range(len(grid) - 1) for c in range(len(grid[0]))) :: minimum_operations([[2], [1]])
edge_count: 2
complexity: time=O(m × n) | space=O(1)
complexity_options: O(m × n); O(m + n); O(m × n × V)
complexity_note: m is the number of rows, n the number of columns, and V the biggest value.
why_time: Each cell is looked at once, and its operations are counted with one subtraction instead of done one by one.
