hint: For each column c, set `prev = grid[0][c]`, then loop r from 1 to the last row.
hint: `need = max(grid[r][c], prev + 1)`; add `need - grid[r][c]` to the total and set prev to need.
right: Columns don't affect each other, and raising each cell only as far as it must keeps every later cell's target as low as possible, so one walk down each column finds the minimum.
