why_space: The answer holds every number.
hint: Loop `for s in range(rows + cols - 1):` and work out top and bottom.
hint: For even s, loop r from bottom down to top; for odd s, from top to bottom. Append `mat[r][s - r]`.
right: Each anti-diagonal is one key r + c, and its row limits come straight from that key, so the walk never steps outside the grid or visits a cell twice.
