fail[2]: The wall ends up as 1, 3, 3 over 1, 1, 1: the second paint adds 2 to row 0, columns 1 and 2.
fail[3]: No paints: everything is 0.
fail[4]: Two tiles end up at 2 − 3 = −1, so the total is 12 × 2 − 6 = 18.
fail[5]: The paint covers the bottom-right tile, so its corners at r2 + 1 and c2 + 1 fall in the extra row and column of d.
